-- title:
--   Faithful flatness from flat algebras reviving each maximal ideal
-- statement:
--   Let $B$ be a commutative ring and let $H$ be an additive commutative group equipped with a $B$-module structure (the ring $B$ and the module $H$ may live in different universes). Assume that for every maximal ideal $M$ of $B$ there exist a type $C$ in the same universe as $B$, a commutative ring structure on $C$, a $B$-algebra structure on $C$ making $C$ flat as a $B$-module, such that two conditions hold: the ideal $M \cdot C$ generated by the image of $M$ under the structure map $B \to C$ is a proper ideal of $C$, and the base change $C \otimes_B H$ is faithfully flat as a $C$-module. Then $H$ is faithfully flat as a $B$-module. Note that no coherence between the algebras $C$ attached to the various maximal ideals is required, and the algebras are not assumed faithfully flat over $B$, only flat with $M \cdot C \neq C$.
--
--   This is the general form of the statement that faithful flatness descends along a family of flat algebras that revive every closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} B$; the familiar case is $C$ a localisation. It is used to establish faithful flatness of a Hopf kernel from the faithful flatness of its base changes to local rings, in [`HopfAlgebra.faithfullyFlat_hopfKer_of_forall_isLocalRing_faithfullyFlat_baseChange`](thm.html#HopfAlgebra.faithfullyFlat_hopfKer_of_forall_isLocalRing_faithfullyFlat_baseChange).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Module_FaithfullyFlat_of_forall_isMaximal_exists_flat_algebra.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

universe u v

theorem Module.FaithfullyFlat.of_forall_isMaximal_exists_flat_algebra
    (B : Type u) [CommRing B] (H : Type v) [AddCommGroup H] [Module B H]
    (h : ∀ (M : Ideal B), M.IsMaximal →
      ∃ (C : Type u) (_ : CommRing C) (_ : Algebra B C) (_ : Module.Flat B C),
        M.map (algebraMap B C) ≠ ⊤ ∧ Module.FaithfullyFlat C (TensorProduct B C H)) :
    Module.FaithfullyFlat B H := by sorry
